        <article class="lesson-article">
            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 4</span><h1>Docker Fundamentals</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>30 min</span><span class="lesson-level advanced">Advanced</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Core Concepts</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Image:</strong> Read-only template with OS, runtime, app code</li>
                        <li><strong>Container:</strong> Running instance of an image</li>
                        <li><strong>Registry:</strong> Storage for images (Docker Hub, ACR, ECR)</li>
                        <li><strong>Dockerfile:</strong> Script to build an image</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Essential Commands</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"># Pull an image
docker pull mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:8.0

# Run a container
docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name myapp myimage

# List containers
docker ps        # running
docker ps -a     # all

# Stop and remove
docker stop myapp
docker rm myapp

# Build an image
docker build -t myapp:1.0 .

# View logs
docker logs myapp -f</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Volumes</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"># Named volume (Docker managed)
docker run -v mydata:/app/data myimage

# Bind mount (host directory)
docker run -v /host/path:/container/path myimage

# Volume for SQL Server
docker run -v sqldata:/var/opt/mssql \
    -e 'ACCEPT_EULA=Y' \
    -e 'SA_PASSWORD=YourPassword123!' \
    -p 1433:1433 \
    mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Networks</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"># Create network
docker network create mynetwork

# Run containers on same network
docker run -d --network mynetwork --name db postgres
docker run -d --network mynetwork --name api myapi

# Containers can reach each other by name
# api can connect to "db:5432"</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
                    <div class="takeaways">
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>Images are templates; containers are running instances.</span></div>
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>Use volumes for persistent data.</span></div>
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>Networks enable container-to-container communication.</span></div>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </div>
